      "text": "### \"People We Meet on Vacation\" by Emily Henry\n\n**Publication Details:**\n- **Year of Publication:** 2021\n- **Publisher:** Berkley\n- **ISBN:** 978-0-593-33489-2\n- **Word Count:** Approximately 94,000 words\n\n**Overview:**\n\"People We Meet on Vacation\" is a contemporary romance that follows two best friends, Alex and Poppy, who have taken an annual vacation together for a decade. The story is structured with alternating timelines—one set in the present ('now') and the other set two years prior. This dual-timeline technique explores the evolution and collapse of their friendship, focusing on themes of self-discovery, grief, regret, and the potential for second chances in love.\n\n**Reception:**\nThe novel has received positive acclaim for its witty banter, emotional depth, and innovative structure. Critics and readers have particularly noted its exploration of the transition from friendship to romance. It has been widely reviewed in multiple major outlets and has solidified its position as a significant work in the romance genre.\n\n**Where It Fits in Emily Henry's Bibliography:**\n\"People We Meet on Vacation\" is one of Emily Henry's notable works, contributing to her recognition as a leading voice in contemporary romance. It follows her previously successful novel, \"Beach Read,\" and continues to showcase her talent for blending humor with emotional storytelling.\n\nFor further details, you might explore the following resources:\n- [Wikipedia Page on People We Meet on Vacation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People_We_Meet_on_Vacation)\n- [Critical Overview](https://example.com/reviews/people-we-meet-on-vacation)\n- [Publisher Page](https://example.com/books/people-we-meet-on-vacation)\n\nThis should provide a comprehensive background for your review on Emily Henry's trajectory as a romance author!",
